      "id": "da72e4c2-3ece-4dcb-97d7-9650da64d263",
      "kind": "problem",
      "theorem_name": "OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction.actual_minor_arithmetic_lower_bound_source017",
      "theorem_title": "Arithmetic lower bound for a nonzero selected interpolation minor",
      "formal_statement": "theorem OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction.actual_minor_arithmetic_lower_bound_source017 {nu : ℝ} (d : FixedData nu)\r\n    (H : ℝ) (hH : 0 < H) (selection : Row d H → Column d H)\r\n    (hdet : (actualMinor d H selection).det ≠ 0) :\r\n    -(1 - actualMean d H) - d.arithmeticError ≤\r\n      Real.log ‖(actualMinor d H selection).det‖ /\r\n        ((actualRowCount d H : ℝ) * H) := by\n  sorry\n",
      "natural_language_statement": "For fixed approximation data $d$, a positive interpolation scale $H$, and a selection of columns whose interpolation minor has nonzero determinant, let $b(H)$ be the actual mean row weight and $M(H)$ the actual row count. The source arithmetic estimate gives\n\n$$-\\bigl(1-b(H)\\bigr)-e_{\\mathrm{ar}}(d)\\le \\frac{\\log|\\det A_{\\mathrm{minor}}(H)|}{M(H)H}.$$\n\nHere $e_{\\mathrm{ar}}(d)$ is the arithmetic error stored in the campaign's original fixed data. This is the exact original source interface, currently published as an Open dependency for the NoFixedData reduction.",
      "definitions": "import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_ApproximationDefinitions\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_DeterminantContradiction_CoreData\n\nopen OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction\n\n",
      "source": "https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Approximation/DeterminantContradiction.lean#L74-L85",
